        explanation: 'It is valid \u2014 multi-provider is exactly when some prescription names a provider different from another of the patient\'s prescriptions, so the EXISTS returns the same five patients. The cost is that it evaluates a correlated EXISTS per row and re-derives rx_count with a scalar subquery, doing more work than the single GROUP BY + HAVING aggregate pass. Same answer, higher cost; the aggregate form is preferable at scale.',
