    debrief: 'The bug is missing the +1 for the initial dispense. A prescription with 2 refills = 1 original fill + 2 refills = 3 total fills. The broken formula calculates days_supply * refills (2 fills), undercounting by one fill period per prescription. Patient 2\'s Metformin: 90 days × 2 refills = 180 days (broken) vs 90 days × (1+2) = 270 days (correct). The Sertraline: 30 × 5 = 150 (broken) vs 30 × 6 = 180 (correct). Total: 330 broken vs 450 correct.\n\n**Why it compounds:** unlike a constant error, this one scales with days_supply. A 90-day medication is understated by 90 days per prescription. A patient on three 90-day chronic medications is understated by 270 days — nearly an entire year of coverage. Outreach calls are being scheduled too early for every patient on long-supply medications.\n\n**The formula to remember:** total fills = 1 + refills. Coverage days = days_supply × (1 + refills). The +1 is always required.',
