    prompt: 'The finance team\'s completed revenue report has been feeding the monthly board deck for two months. This month a new analyst cross-checked the number against payment processor records and found it $130 higher than expected. Identify the discrepancy and write a corrected query to calculate the accurate revenue.',
    brokenQuery: 'SELECT ROUND((SUM(o.subtotal))::numeric, 2) AS total_revenue\nFROM orders o\nJOIN order_items oi ON o.order_id = oi.order_id\nWHERE o.status = \'completed\'',
    brokenOutputNote: 'Returns $2,459.75 — inflated by $130 vs the correct $2,329.75. Two orders have multiple line items. When you JOIN to order_items, those orders appear twice in the result set and their subtotals are counted twice.',
    expectedColumns: ['total_revenue'],
    expectedRowCount: 1,
    hintSteps: [
      { text: 'Consider the data flow from orders to revenue calculation. Check if there\'s an unintended aggregation or filtering step that could inflate the total.', starterCode: 'SELECT ROUND(SUM(subtotal), 2) AS total_revenue FROM orders WHERE status = \'completed\';' },
      { text: 'Examine how the subtotal is calculated. Ensure that it\'s not being inflated by additional factors like discounts or shipping costs that shouldn\'t be included.', starterCode: 'SELECT ROUND(SUM(subtotal), 2) AS total_revenue FROM orders WHERE status = \'completed\';' }
    ],
