    prompt: 'The marketing team reports that paid and organic campaigns reached 15 users combined. The platform has only 15 registered users total, so 100% reach would require every user to have a session from one of those two channels. The number is implausible. Find the bug.',
    brokenQuery: 'SELECT COUNT(*) AS total_reached_users\nFROM (\n  SELECT user_id FROM sessions WHERE source = \'paid\'\n  UNION ALL\n  SELECT user_id FROM sessions WHERE source = \'organic\'\n)',
    brokenOutputNote: 'Returns 15 — the total row count from both subqueries combined. User 5 has both paid and organic sessions and is counted twice. Users with multiple sessions per channel are also counted multiple times. UNION ALL preserves all duplicates.',
