        stem: 'Two restaurants tie on revenue at the 5th spot and the spec says \'show every restaurant in the top 5, including ties\'. ROW_NUMBER with rn <= 5 returns 5 rows; RANK with rk <= 5 returns 6. Which is correct and why?',
        options: ['rank_filter', 'row_number', 'orderby_limit', 'no_delivered_filter'],
        answerId: 'rank_filter',
        explanation: 'RANK gives tied restaurants the same rank, so rk <= 5 keeps both restaurants tied at rank 5 — 6 rows — which matches \'include ties\'. ROW_NUMBER assigns a strict 1..N sequence and would cut to exactly 5, dropping one tied restaurant arbitrarily (no secondary sort key = engine-dependent pick), which violates the spec. ORDER BY + LIMIT 5 has the same arbitrary-cut problem as ROW_NUMBER. On this seed the top-5 revenues are distinct so all three agree; the divergence is a tie-only fork — pick by whether the spec wants \'exactly 5\' or \'all tied winners\'.',
